// DOCKER IMAGES — pull public, save/load everything else
// ===========================================================================
/**
 * Make one image exist on the TARGET.
 *
 *   already present → nothing (a re-run must not re-transfer gigabytes)
 *   public registry → `docker pull` (fast, and costs no source bandwidth)
 *   otherwise       → `docker save | gzip` on the source, streamed straight
 *                     through the SSH channel into `gunzip | docker load`
 *
 * The locally-built case is the one that silently broke a real migration: the
 * engine copied files and named volumes but never the IMAGE, so standalone
 * containers could never start. A pull that fails also falls back to save/load,
 * so a private registry the new box cannot authenticate to still works.
 *
